Overview
This tutorial will be split in three main parts:

“R packages version management with renv”, which covers {renv} for R packages version management;
“Building analysis pipelines with targets”, which covers the {targets} R package for structuring the analysis code in a clean and modular way;
“Containerizing working environment for cross-platform reproducibility”, which covers Docker (using Binder) for building containers that include all operating system files, R installation, any additional system dependencies. Binder allows your code immediately reproducible by anyone, anywhere through a simple browser.

3.5 Set the working directory
WORKDIR ${HOME}
${NB_USER} and ${HOME} are environment variables already defined by the rocker/binder base image (NB_USER=rstudio, HOME=/home/rstudio). Using the variables instead of hardcoding /home/rstudio keeps the Dockerfile portable if the base image’s user ever changes.

3.8 Copy the rest of the repository
COPY --chown=${NB_USER} . ${HOME}
With packages already installed, we bring in everything else — the scripts, _targets.R, data folders, all of it. Because this happens after the cached restore layer, changing any of these files and rebuilding only re-runs this COPY and nothing above it.
